dest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Flowco Holdings Inc. is a small-cap energy business with a $1.8B market cap on $760M of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at 38% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 28-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $167M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 22 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 7.11\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","Accruals are elevated at -15.4% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 7.9\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 2.6% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 3.3% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.8\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.4% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $192.5M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-192525001.47},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Energy tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","